          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly avows the narrator's present love for Maria. It answers her request for assurance that his apparent change is genuine and not something he will regret tomorrow.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke\\nnoget, Du nu bilder Dig ind, fordi Du har længtes en Smule efter din\\nElskerinde?«\\n\\nJeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"The exact focal expression is an avowal, not by itself an undertaking to perform an action or assume an obligation. The continuation introduces constancy and a hoped-for shared life, but that neighbouring material should not be transferred onto the marked words as their core force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is intensely emotional, the focal words occur in a deliberate, reasoned answer to Maria's question. They are not represented as a reflex-like cry or affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"No independent residual force is needed: the focal expression is adequately characterized as a direct avowal of love. Its reassuring function is achieved through that avowal rather than through a separate speech-act mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke\\nnoget, Du nu bilder Dig ind\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"fordi hun forstaar, jeg\\ntaler sandt\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At an emotional reunion, Maria asks the unnamed narrator whether his apparent love is genuine, lasting, and not merely caused by temporary longing for his lover. He responds directly to her with the marked avowal.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal words themselves undertake nothing beyond presenting his love as true. The surrounding continuation—especially “Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i Nød, Hverdage og Festdage” and his wish to live a long time with Maria—adds constancy and shared-future colouring, but its precise status as a promise or obligation is not explicit. Maria accepts the avowal as truthful and responds with happy tears: “hun forstaar, jeg taler sandt, og fordi hun er lykkelig.”\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the work with sufficient confidence from the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly supports the represented sincerity of the avowal and Maria's acceptance of it, but it does not independently establish formal terms of commitment or later fulfilment.\"}"
        }
